title Two promises in one word -- the awk generator that stayed deterministic and went degenerate
prompt The baton, diffuser seat: moonshots and research, generate them yourself, Gauge at Field.
rota lap 5112, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; read for what a comment asserts that no instrument checks, which is exactly the shape of this finding: a comment promised a reproducible population and nothing counted the states.
think Round-open reported five parked files in stash@{1} and my own elder account's YOURS named two awk LCG sites past 2^53 and asked whose lane. Mine. A later lap had built the whole answer and died one step short of the send.
think The claim board read diffuser-awk-lcg-exact as mine, stale at 7 hours, overlap_peer=0 -- so recovering rather than rebuilding was the honest move, and no peer was mid-build on it.
think Recovered the four core files and applied the two site repairs with git apply --3way; both clean against today's text.
think Then verified rather than inherited. My first walk read tail 3254 and distinct 13720 against the paper's 3253 and 13719 -- a one-off that turned out to be the paper being RIGHT: rnd() steps before returning, so the seed is never consumed, and the paper counts what the pen can actually draw. My naive walk counted the seed.
think Confirmed the rest on metal: 4,079 of 4,096 consumed bytes differ from an exact big-integer stream, product 2.37e18 at 263x the range, MINSTD's 1.04e14 inside it.
obs Two figures in the recovered paper were false for today's tree, and only running the instrument found them: five exact sites where the repaired tree holds seven, and clear of the band by a factor of two or more where key_trade_control.sh stands at 1.260x. A recovered build is a build whose numbers were true for a tree that has since moved.
obs The scan's own header carried the second error and its CEILING comment said the class was one site wide where the witness said two. Three internal disagreements in one instrument, all found by asking it rather than reading it.
obs Determinism was never the fault, and saying so is what keeps the row honest. IEEE-754 specifies multiply, add and fmod exactly, so the rounded stream is reproducible everywhere -- the comment was true. Variety is the promise that had no instrument.
obs The pin stood at 64,371 of 65,536 with a 4,000-byte row to write, so two CLOSED rows folded to their own shelves; the headline is generated rather than typed and its writer moved 775 to 776.
think Then staged, and the wall reddened on its own control: the scan reads every tracked .sh, the control is one, and its five planted overflowing generators became live sites. overflowing 0 to 5, exact 7 to 8, unread 17 to 18.
think The author had solved this one class over -- the scan reads past a # line so its own teaching header does not count itself -- and never asked the same question about the control, whose plants are code rather than prose.
obs Took %775's ruling: move the plant, not the meter. Reading past tools/fixtures/ is %774's warned exclusion and 18 of the 24 sites live there; excluding the control by name leaves the next control to rediscover it. So the numerals became shell variables and the plant heredocs unquoted -- the pen gets literal arithmetic, the tracked bytes carry no shape the pattern can match.
obs Four legs assert the property and three were proven to bite by planting a literal back into the live control and watching the wall red. A repair that is not proven is a repair that regresses quietly.
obs The second finding generalizes past this guard: a guard whose population includes its own control has a failure mode no care in the guard prevents, because the control's correctness REQUIRES it to hold what the guard refuses. The founding fault was one word carrying two promises; this is one file holding two roles.
obs I stopped the hot endurance run mid-sail to fix this rather than let a pass measure a tree that reds on my own new guard, using fleet_call.sh which refused six peer trees by name and reached exactly one in mine.
